IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-part16-interim-release.l4 -- sections 515 (except (4.1) to (4.4), (6), (6.1), (7) and (10), which are in ccc20-part16-reverse-onus.l4) to 519.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada): judicial interim release.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a "may" whose gate is "where",
-- "when" or "upon" answers JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) and is counted in the fork register; a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails.
-- The answers of other parts are inputs named for the section that answers them: `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (MAYBE BOOLEAN). The answer of subsection (6) (a function of
-- ccc20-part16-reverse-onus.l4) is an input here, so that this module does not import that one.

§ `Section 515(1) and (2) -- The release order`

-- src:11366 | Release order without conditions
-- src:11367 | 515 (1) Subject to this section, when an accused who is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469 is taken before a justice, the justice shall, unless a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted, make a release order in respect of that offence, without conditions, unless the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause, in respect of that offence, why the detention of the accused in custody is justified or why an order under any other provision of this section should be made.
-- src:11368 | Release order with conditions
-- src:11369 | (2) If the justice does not make an order under subsection (1), the justice shall, unless the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused is justified, make a release order that sets out the conditions directed by the justice under subsection (4) and, as the case may be,
-- src:11370 | (a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations;
-- src:11371 | (b) the accused’s promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order;
-- src:11372 | (c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused’s promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order;
-- src:11373 | (d) the obligation to deposit money or other valuable security in a specified amount or value, with or without the accused’s promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order; or
-- src:11374 | (e) if the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province in which they are in custody or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody, the obligation to deposit money or other valuable security in a specified amount or value, with or without the accused’s promise to pay a specified amount by the justice if they fail to comply with a condition of the order and with or without sureties.
@ref s 515(1) and (2) (src:11366-11374)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is taken before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified or why an order under any other provision of this section should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an accused who is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an accused who is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469"
        IF NOT `the accused is taken before a justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when an accused ... is taken before a justice, the justice shall"
        IF `a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted"
        IF `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified or why an order under any other provision of this section should be made`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 515(2)(a) to (e) the financial terms (src:11370-11374)
DECLARE `s 515(2) the financial term of the release order` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations`
    `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order`
    `s 515(2)(c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount`
    `s 515(2)(d) the obligation to deposit money or other valuable security in a specified amount or value, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount`
    `s 515(2)(e) the obligation of an accused who is not ordinarily resident in the province, or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres, to deposit money or other valuable security, with or without a promise to pay and with or without sureties`

@ref s 515(2) (src:11368-11369)
GIVEN `the justice does not make an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused is justified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2) the justice must make a release order that sets out the conditions directed under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the justice does not make an order under subsection (1)` AND NOT `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused is justified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the justice does not make an order under subsection (1), the justice shall, unless the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused is justified, make a release order"

@ref s 515(2)(a) to (e) (src:11370-11374)
GIVEN term IS A `s 515(2) the financial term of the release order`
      `the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province in which they are in custody or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` MEANS
    IF term EQUALS `s 515(2)(e) the obligation of an accused who is not ordinarily resident in the province, or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres, to deposit money or other valuable security, with or without a promise to pay and with or without sureties`
       AND NOT `the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province in which they are in custody or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province in which they are in custody or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody" (an "if" gate on a term the order may set out)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The core's `Outcome of interim release` has four values. The terms of paragraph (2)(c) (sureties) are "release on a release order with conditions and a surety"; the others of (2) are "release on a release order with
-- conditions" (ASSUMED, not ruled: paragraph (2)(e) "with or without sureties" is mapped to "with conditions"; the deposit forms (d) and (e) have no variant of their own in the core: NEEDS-CORE.md).
@ref s 515(2) the outcome (src:11367-11374)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 515(6) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor shows cause why an order under a provision of section 515 other than subsection (1) should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      term IS A `s 515(2) the financial term of the release order`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Outcome of interim release`
`s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence mentioned in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `detention in custody`   -- the justice "shall order that the accused be detained in custody": subsection (11)
        IF `a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless a plea of guilty by the accused is accepted" (subsection 518(2): the justice "may make any order provided for in this Part")
        IF `the answer of s 515(6) applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if the accused is charged (a) ... (d)" (a limb of subsection (6) rests on an answer outside this range that is not covered)
        IF `the answer of s 515(6) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT `the accused shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified` THEN JUST `detention in custody`   -- subsection (6)
        IF `the answer of s 515(6) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST (`release with conditions` term)   -- subsection (7): the justice "shall make a release order under this section"
        IF `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified` THEN JUST `detention in custody`   -- subsection (5)
        IF `the prosecutor shows cause why an order under a provision of section 515 other than subsection (1) should be made` THEN JUST (`release with conditions` term)   -- subsection (2)
        OTHERWISE JUST `release on a release order without conditions`   -- subsection (1)
    WHERE
        `release with conditions` t MEANS
            IF t EQUALS `s 515(2)(c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount`
            THEN `release on a release order with conditions and a surety`
            ELSE `release on a release order with conditions`

-- The seam answer PLAN.md section 6 asks of this part for s 145: "the accused is bound by a release order": BOOLEAN. True of the three release outcomes, false of detention.
@ref s 515 the accused is bound by a release order (the seam of s 145) (src:11367)
GIVEN outcome IS AN `Outcome of interim release`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN `release on a release order without conditions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `release on a release order with conditions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `release on a release order with conditions and a surety` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `detention in custody` THEN FALSE

-- src:11375 | Imposition of least onerous form of release
-- src:11376 | (2.01) The justice shall not make an order containing the conditions referred to in one of the paragraphs (2)(b) to (e) unless the prosecution shows cause why an order containing the conditions referred to in the preceding paragraphs for any less onerous form of release would be inadequate.
-- src:11377 | Promise to pay favoured over deposit
-- src:11378 | (2.02) The justice shall favour a promise to pay an amount over the deposit of an amount of money if the accused or the surety, if applicable, has reasonably recoverable assets.
-- src:11379 | Restraint in use of surety
-- src:11380 | (2.03) For greater certainty, before making an order requiring that the accused have a surety, the justice shall be satisfied that this requirement is the least onerous form of release possible for the accused in the circumstances.
-- src:11381 | Non-application
-- src:11382 | (2.04) Subsection (2.01) does not apply to an accused to whom subsection (6) applies.
@ref s 515(2.01) to (2.04) (src:11375-11382)
GIVEN term IS A `s 515(2) the financial term of the release order`
      `the prosecution shows cause why an order containing the conditions referred to in the preceding paragraphs for any less onerous form of release would be inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 515(6) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.01) the justice is barred from making an order containing the term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 515(6) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(2.04) Subsection (2.01) does not apply to an accused to whom subsection (6) applies"
        IF `the answer of s 515(6) applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an accused to whom subsection (6) applies" (a limb of subsection (6) rests on an answer outside this range that is not covered)
        IF term EQUALS `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not make an order containing the conditions referred to in one of the paragraphs (2)(b) to (e)" (paragraph (a) is outside the bar)
        IF `the prosecution shows cause why an order containing the conditions referred to in the preceding paragraphs for any less onerous form of release would be inadequate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecution shows cause why an order containing the conditions referred to in the preceding paragraphs for any less onerous form of release would be inadequate"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 515(2.04) (src:11381-11382)
GIVEN `the answer of s 515(6) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.04) subsection (2.01) applies to the accused` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 515(6) applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an accused to whom subsection (6) applies" (a limb of subsection (6) rests on an answer outside this range that is not covered)
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2.01) does not apply to an accused to whom subsection (6) applies"
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2.04) says only that (2.01) does not apply to an accused to whom (6) applies; subsection (2.01) speaks for any other accused

@ref s 515(2.02) (src:11377-11378)
GIVEN `the accused or the surety, if applicable, has reasonably recoverable assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.02) the justice must favour a promise to pay an amount over the deposit of an amount of money` MEANS
    IF `the accused or the surety, if applicable, has reasonably recoverable assets`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The justice shall favour a promise to pay an amount over the deposit of an amount of money if the accused or the surety, if applicable, has reasonably recoverable assets"

@ref s 515(2.03) (src:11379-11380)
GIVEN `the justice is about to make an order requiring that the accused have a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.03) the justice must be satisfied that a surety is the least onerous form of release possible for the accused` MEANS
    IF `the justice is about to make an order requiring that the accused have a surety`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before making an order requiring that the accused have a surety, the justice shall be satisfied that this requirement is the least onerous form of release possible"

-- src:11383 | Power of justice — sureties
-- src:11384 | (2.1) If, under subsection (2) or any other provision of this Act, a judge, justice or court makes a release order with a requirement for sureties, the judge, justice or court may name particular persons as sureties.
@ref s 515(2.1) (src:11383-11384)
GIVEN `a judge, justice or court makes a release order with a requirement for sureties under subsection (2) or any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.1) the judge, justice or court may name particular persons as sureties` MEANS
    IF `a judge, justice or court makes a release order with a requirement for sureties under subsection (2) or any other provision of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, under subsection (2) or any other provision of this Act, a judge, justice or court makes a release order with a requirement for sureties, the judge, justice or court may name particular persons as sureties" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- 515(2.11): "convicted of an indictable offence within ten years before the day on which the release order is made". The conviction's offence is described as s 493.01 does. The ten years are read as including the day
-- ten years before the release order (fork F-ten-years).
-- src:11385 | Prohibition — surety convicted of indictable offence
-- src:11386 | (2.11) Despite subsection (2.1), a judge, justice or court shall not name a person as surety if the person was convicted of an indictable offence within ten years before the day on which the release order is made unless the judge, justice or court is satisfied that no other suitable surety is available and that doing so is in the interests of justice.
@ref s 515(2.11) (src:11385-11386)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `s 493.01 the offence charged`
      `the date of the conviction` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the release order is made` IS A DATE
      `the judge, justice or court is satisfied that no other suitable surety is available and that naming the person is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.11) the judge, justice or court is barred from naming the person as surety` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 493.01 the offence is treated as an indictable offence` `the offence of which the person was convicted`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person was convicted of an indictable offence"
        IF `the date of the conviction` LESS THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the release order is made`) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the release order is made`) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the release order is made` MINUS 10))
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "convicted of an indictable offence within ten years before the day on which the release order is made"
        IF `the judge, justice or court is satisfied that no other suitable surety is available and that naming the person is in the interests of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge, justice or court is satisfied that no other suitable surety is available and that doing so is in the interests of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11387 | Record of reasons for surety
-- src:11388 | (2.12) If a judge, justice or court names a person described in subsection (2.11) as a surety, the judge, justice or court shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for doing so.
@ref s 515(2.12) (src:11387-11388)
GIVEN `the judge, justice or court names a person described in subsection (2.11) as a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.12) the judge, justice or court must include in the record a statement of the reasons for naming the person` MEANS
    IF `the judge, justice or court names a person described in subsection (2.11) as a surety`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a judge, justice or court names a person described in subsection (2.11) as a surety, the judge, justice or court shall include in the record a statement of the reasons"

§ `Section 515(2.2) to (4) -- Appearance, factors and conditions`

-- src:11389 | Appearance of the accused
-- src:11390 | (2.2) If, by this Act, the appearance of an accused is required for the purposes of judicial interim release, the accused shall appear in person but the justice may allow the accused to appear by videoconference or, subject to subsection (2.3), by audioconference, if the technological means is satisfactory to the justice.
-- src:11391 | When consent required for audioconference
-- src:11392 | (2.3) If the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference and the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance, the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is required for the appearance of the accused by audioconference.
@ref s 515(2.2) and (2.3) (src:11389-11392)
GIVEN `the appearance of the accused is required by this Act for the purposes of judicial interim release` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.2) the accused must appear in person` MEANS
    IF `the appearance of the accused is required by this Act for the purposes of judicial interim release`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, by this Act, the appearance of an accused is required for the purposes of judicial interim release, the accused shall appear in person"

@ref s 515(2.2) and (2.3) the audio and video appearance (src:11390-11392)
GIVEN `the appearance of the accused is required by this Act for the purposes of judicial interim release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technological means is satisfactory to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference and the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor and the accused consent to the appearance by audioconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appearance is by audioconference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.2) the justice may allow the accused to appear by videoconference or audioconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appearance of the accused is required by this Act for the purposes of judicial interim release` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, by this Act, the appearance of an accused is required for the purposes of judicial interim release" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        IF NOT `the technological means is satisfactory to the justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice may allow the accused to appear by videoconference or ... by audioconference, if the technological means is satisfactory to the justice" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        IF `the appearance is by audioconference` AND `the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference and the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance` AND NOT `the prosecutor and the accused consent to the appearance by audioconference`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (2.3)" (the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is required)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 515(2.3) (src:11391-11392)
GIVEN `the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(2.3) the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is required for the appearance of the accused by audioconference` MEANS
    IF `the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` AND `the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused cannot appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference and the evidence of a witness is to be taken at the appearance, the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is required"

-- src:11393 | Factors to consider
-- src:11394 | (3) In making an order under this section, the justice shall consider any relevant factors, including,
-- src:11395 | (a) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner;
-- src:11396 | (a.1) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which random and unprovoked violence was used or attempted; or
-- src:11397 | (b) whether the accused has been previously convicted of a criminal offence, including any offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any person.
@ref s 515(3) (src:11393-11397)
DECLARE `s 515(3) a factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(3)(a) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner`
    `s 515(3)(a.1) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which random and unprovoked violence was used or attempted`
    `s 515(3)(b) whether the accused has been previously convicted of a criminal offence, including any offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any person`
    `s 515(3) a factor the text does not name`

@ref s 515(3) (src:11394-11397)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 515(3) a factor`
      `the factor is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(3) the justice must consider the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 515(3)(a) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(3)(a.1) whether the accused is charged with an offence in the commission of which random and unprovoked violence was used or attempted` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(3)(b) whether the accused has been previously convicted of a criminal offence, including any offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(3) a factor the text does not name` THEN
        IF `the factor is relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the justice shall consider any relevant factors, including" names three factors and says nothing of a factor that is not relevant

-- src:11398 | Conditions authorized
-- src:11399 | (4) When making an order under subsection (2), the justice may direct the accused to comply with one or more of the following conditions specified in the order:
-- src:11400 | (a) report at specified times to a peace officer, or other person, designated in the order;
-- src:11401 | (b) remain within a specified territorial jurisdiction;
-- src:11402 | (c) notify a peace officer or other person designated in the order of any change in their address, employment or occupation;
-- src:11403 | (d) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:11404 | (e) abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:11405 | (f) deposit all their passports as specified in the order;
-- src:11406 | (g) comply with any other specified condition that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence; and
-- src:11407 | (h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable.
@ref s 515(4) (src:11398-11407)
DECLARE `s 515(4) the condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(4)(a) report at specified times to a peace officer, or other person, designated in the order`
    `s 515(4)(b) remain within a specified territorial jurisdiction`
    `s 515(4)(c) notify a peace officer or other person designated in the order of any change in their address, employment or occupation`
    `s 515(4)(d) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order`
    `s 515(4)(e) abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order`
    `s 515(4)(f) deposit all their passports as specified in the order`
    `s 515(4)(g) comply with any other specified condition that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
    `s 515(4)(h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable`

@ref s 515(4) (src:11398-11399)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      condition IS A `s 515(4) the condition`
      `the justice considers the condition necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is reasonable and the justice considers it desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice makes an order under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When making an order under subsection (2), the justice may direct the accused to comply with one or more of the following conditions" (a "when" gate on a "may": the periods ruling (b) and the delegated ruling (c) say JUST FALSE; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)
        IF condition EQUALS `s 515(4)(g) comply with any other specified condition that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
           AND NOT `the justice considers the condition necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(g) comply with any other specified condition that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 515(4)(h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable`
           AND NOT `the condition is reasonable and the justice considers it desirable`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 515(5) and (9) to (14.1) -- Detention, reasons and copies`

-- src:11446 | Detention in custody
-- src:11447 | (5) Where the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified, the justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody until he is dealt with according to law and shall include in the record a statement of his reasons for making the order.
@ref s 515(5) (src:11446-11447)
GIVEN `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(5) the justice must order that the accused be detained in custody and state the reasons in the record` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified, the justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody"

-- src:11478 | Sufficiency of record
-- src:11479 | (9) For the purposes of subsections (5) and (6), it is sufficient if a record is made of the reasons in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries.
-- src:11480 | Written reasons
-- src:11481 | (9.1) Despite subsection (9), if the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody primarily because of a previous conviction of the accused, the justice shall state that reason, in writing, in the record.
@ref s 515(9) and (9.1) (src:11478-11481)
GIVEN `a record of the reasons is made in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(9) it is sufficient for the purposes of subsections (5) and (6) that a record is made in accordance with Part XVIII` MEANS
    IF `a record of the reasons is made in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is sufficient if a record is made of the reasons in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII" (the text says a record so made is sufficient and does not say that no other is)

@ref s 515(9.1) (src:11480-11481)
GIVEN `the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody primarily because of a previous conviction of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(9.1) the justice must state in writing, in the record, that the detention is ordered primarily because of a previous conviction` MEANS
    IF `the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody primarily because of a previous conviction of the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody primarily because of a previous conviction of the accused, the justice shall state that reason, in writing, in the record"

-- src:11492 | Detention in custody for offence listed in section 469
-- src:11493 | (11) Where an accused who is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 is taken before a justice, the justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody until he is dealt with according to law and shall issue a warrant in Form 8 for the committal of the accused.
@ref s 515(11) (src:11492-11493)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is taken before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(11) the justice must order that the accused be detained in custody and issue a warrant in Form 8 for the committal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence mentioned in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the accused is taken before a justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused who is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 is taken before a justice, the justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody"

-- src:11494 | Order re no communication
-- src:11495 | (12) A justice who orders that an accused be detained in custody under this section may include in the order a direction that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order, except in accordance with such conditions specified in the order as the justice considers necessary.
@ref s 515(12) (src:11494-11495)
GIVEN `the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(12) the justice may include in the order a direction that the accused abstain from communicating with any victim, witness or other person` MEANS
    IF `the justice orders that the accused be detained in custody under section 515`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice who orders that an accused be detained in custody under this section may include in the order a direction" (a "may" for a justice who orders detention)

-- src:11496 | Victim’s and community’s safety and security
-- src:11497 | (13) A justice who makes an order under this section shall include in the record of the proceedings a statement that the justice considered the safety and security of every victim of the offence and the safety and security of the community when making the order.
@ref s 515(13) (src:11496-11497)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(13) the justice must include in the record a statement that the justice considered the safety and security of every victim and of the community` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order under section 515`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who makes an order under this section shall include in the record of the proceedings a statement that the justice considered the safety and security of every victim of the offence and the safety and security of the community"

-- src:11498 | Aboriginal accused or vulnerable populations
-- src:11499 | (13.1) A justice who makes an order under this section shall include in the record of proceedings a statement that sets out both how they determined whether the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2 and their determination. If the justice determines that the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2, they shall also include a statement indicating how they considered their particular circumstances, as required under that section.
@ref s 515(13.1) (src:11498-11499)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice determines that the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(13.1) the justice must include in the record a statement of how the justice determined whether the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2, and the determination` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order under section 515`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who makes an order under this section shall include in the record of proceedings a statement that sets out both how they determined whether the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2 and their determination"

@ref s 515(13.1) the second sentence (src:11499)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice determines that the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(13.1) the justice must also include a statement of how the justice considered the accused's particular circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order under section 515` AND `the justice determines that the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the justice determines that the accused is an accused referred to in section 493.2, they shall also include a statement indicating how they considered their particular circumstances"

-- src:11500 | Copy to victim
-- src:11501 | (14) If an order is made under this section, the justice shall, on request by a victim of the offence, cause a copy of the order to be given to the victim.
@ref s 515(14) (src:11500-11501)
GIVEN `an order is made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a victim of the offence requests a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(14) the justice must cause a copy of the order to be given to the victim` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under section 515` AND `a victim of the offence requests a copy of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under this section, the justice shall, on request by a victim of the offence, cause a copy of the order to be given to the victim"

-- src:11502 | Inquiry for copies
-- src:11503 | (14.1) Upon making an order under subsection (2), the justice must ask the prosecutor whether victims of the offence have been informed of their right to request a copy of the order.
@ref s 515(14.1) (src:11502-11503)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(14.1) the justice must ask the prosecutor whether victims of the offence have been informed of their right to request a copy` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon making an order under subsection (2), the justice must ask the prosecutor whether victims of the offence have been informed of their right to request a copy of the order"

§ `Sections 515.01 and 515.1 -- Identification attendance and the surety's declaration`

-- src:11504 | Attendance — Identification of Criminals Act
-- src:11505 | 515.01 When a release order is made under section 515, the judge or justice may also make an order, in Form 11.1, requiring the accused to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act if the accused is charged with an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act.
@ref s 515.01 (src:11504-11505)
GIVEN `a release order is made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is charged with an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515.01 the judge or justice may make an order in Form 11.1 requiring the accused to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a release order is made under section 515` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a release order is made under section 515, the judge or justice may also make an order, in Form 11.1" (a "when" gate on a "may": ruling (b) and (c); the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is charged with an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11506 | Declaration of surety
-- src:11507 | 515.1 (1) Before a judge, justice or court names a particular person as a surety, the person shall provide the judge, justice or court with a signed declaration under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation in Form 12 that sets out
-- src:11508 | (a) their name, date of birth and contact information;
-- src:11509 | (b) information demonstrating that they are suitable to act as a surety for the accused, including financial information;
-- src:11510 | (c) their relationship to the accused;
-- src:11511 | (d) the name and date of birth of any other accused for whom they act as a surety;
-- src:11512 | (e) their acknowledgment of the charge, and of any other outstanding charges against the accused and the contents of the accused’s criminal record, if any;
-- src:11513 | (f) their acknowledgment of the amount that they are willing to promise to pay or deposit to the court and that may be forfeited if the accused fails to comply with any condition of the release order;
-- src:11514 | (g) their acknowledgment that they understand the role and responsibilities of a surety and that they assume these voluntarily; and
-- src:11515 | (h) a description of the contents of their criminal record and any outstanding charges against them, if any.
@ref s 515.1(1) (src:11506-11515)
GIVEN `the judge, justice or court names a particular person as a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is signed, under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation, in Form 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the person's name, date of birth and contact information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out information demonstrating that the person is suitable to act as a surety for the accused, including financial information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the person's relationship to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the name and date of birth of any other accused for whom the person acts as a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the person's acknowledgment of the charge, of any other outstanding charges against the accused and of the contents of the accused's criminal record, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the person's acknowledgment of the amount that they are willing to promise to pay or deposit to the court and that may be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the person's acknowledgment that they understand the role and responsibilities of a surety and that they assume these voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out a description of the contents of the person's criminal record and any outstanding charges against them, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515.1(1) the person has provided the declaration the subsection requires before being named as a surety` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge, justice or court names a particular person as a surety` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before a judge, justice or court names a particular person as a surety, the person shall provide"
        IF `the declaration is signed, under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation, in Form 12`
           AND `it sets out the person's name, date of birth and contact information`   -- (a)
           AND `it sets out information demonstrating that the person is suitable to act as a surety for the accused, including financial information`   -- (b)
           AND `it sets out the person's relationship to the accused`   -- (c)
           AND `it sets out the name and date of birth of any other accused for whom the person acts as a surety`   -- (d)
           AND `it sets out the person's acknowledgment of the charge, of any other outstanding charges against the accused and of the contents of the accused's criminal record, if any`   -- (e)
           AND `it sets out the person's acknowledgment of the amount that they are willing to promise to pay or deposit to the court and that may be forfeited`   -- (f)
           AND `it sets out the person's acknowledgment that they understand the role and responsibilities of a surety and that they assume these voluntarily`   -- (g)
           AND `it sets out a description of the contents of the person's criminal record and any outstanding charges against them, if any`   -- (h)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person shall provide the judge, justice or court with a signed declaration under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation in Form 12 that sets out (a) ... (h)"

-- src:11516 | Exception
-- src:11517 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a judge, justice or court may name a person as a surety without a declaration if
-- src:11518 | (a) the prosecutor consents to it; or
-- src:11519 | (b) the judge, justice or court is satisfied that
-- src:11520 | (i) the person cannot reasonably provide a declaration in the circumstances,
-- src:11521 | (ii) the judge, justice or court has received sufficient information of the kind that would be set out in a declaration to evaluate whether the person is suitable to act as a surety for the accused, and
-- src:11522 | (iii) the person has acknowledged that they have received sufficient information with respect to the matters referred to in paragraphs (1)(e) to (g) to accept the role and responsibilities of a surety.
@ref s 515.1(2) (src:11516-11522)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, justice or court is satisfied that the person cannot reasonably provide a declaration in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, justice or court has received sufficient information of the kind that would be set out in a declaration to evaluate whether the person is suitable to act as a surety for the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has acknowledged that they have received sufficient information with respect to the matters referred to in paragraphs (1)(e) to (g) to accept the role and responsibilities of a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515.1(2) the judge, justice or court may name the person as a surety without a declaration` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor consents to it`   -- (a)
       OR (   `the judge, justice or court is satisfied that the person cannot reasonably provide a declaration in the circumstances`   -- (b)(i)
          AND `the judge, justice or court has received sufficient information of the kind that would be set out in a declaration to evaluate whether the person is suitable to act as a surety for the accused`   -- (b)(ii)
          AND `the person has acknowledged that they have received sufficient information with respect to the matters referred to in paragraphs (1)(e) to (g) to accept the role and responsibilities of a surety`)   -- (b)(iii)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge, justice or court may name a person as a surety without a declaration if (a) the prosecutor consents to it; or (b) ..." (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11523 | Means of telecommunication
-- src:11524 | (3) A person may provide the judge, justice or court with the declaration referred to in subsection (1) by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref s 515.1(3) (src:11523-11524)
GIVEN `the declaration is provided by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515.1(3) the person may provide the declaration by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is provided by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may provide the judge, justice or court with the declaration referred to in subsection (1) by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing"

§ `Sections 516 to 519.1 -- Adjournment, publication, evidence and the release itself`

-- src:11525 | Adjournment of proceedings
-- src:11526 | 516 A justice may, before or at any time during the course of any proceedings under section 515, on application by the prosecutor or the accused, adjourn the proceedings and remand the accused to custody in prison by warrant in Form 19, but no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days except with the consent of the accused.
@ref s 516 (src:11525-11526)
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516 the justice may adjourn the proceedings and remand the accused to custody in prison by warrant in Form 19` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the prosecutor or the accused, adjourn the proceedings" (an "on" gate on a "may": the delegated ruling (c) counts "upon" as "where"; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings under section 515` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice may, before or at any time during the course of any proceedings under section 515" (a scope limit, read as in s 518(1): "In any proceedings under section 515"; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days except with the consent of the accused". The text gives no rule for counting clear days, so the caller states the number of clear days.
@ref s 516 the limit (src:11526)
GIVEN `the clear days of the adjournment` IS A NUMBER
      `the accused consents to a longer adjournment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516 the adjournment is not for more than three clear days, or the accused consents` MEANS
    IF `the clear days of the adjournment` AT MOST 3 OR `the accused consents to a longer adjournment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days except with the consent of the accused"

-- src:11527 | Remand in custody — non-communication order
-- src:11528 | 516.1 (1) A justice who remands an accused to custody under subsection 503(3) or 515(11) or section 516 may order that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order, except in accordance with any conditions specified in the order that the justice considers necessary.
-- src:11529 | Duration of order
-- src:11530 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) remains in force,
-- src:11531 | (a) until it is varied or revoked;
-- src:11532 | (b) until an order in respect of the accused is made under section 515;
-- src:11533 | (c) until the accused is acquitted of the offence, if applicable; or
-- src:11534 | (d) until the time the accused is sentenced, if applicable.
@ref s 516.1 (src:11527-11534)
GIVEN `the justice remands the accused to custody under subsection 503(3) or 515(11) or section 516` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516.1(1) the justice may order that the accused abstain from communicating with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice remands the accused to custody under subsection 503(3) or 515(11) or section 516`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice who remands an accused to custody under subsection 503(3) or 515(11) or section 516 may order" (a "may" for a justice who so remands)

@ref s 516.1(2) (src:11530-11534)
GIVEN `the order has been varied or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order in respect of the accused has been made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been acquitted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516.1(2) the order remains in force` MEANS
    IF `the order has been varied or revoked` OR `an order in respect of the accused has been made under section 515` OR `the accused has been acquitted of the offence` OR `the accused has been sentenced`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under subsection (1) remains in force, (a) until it is varied or revoked; (b) until an order in respect of the accused is made under section 515; (c) until the accused is acquitted of the offence, if applicable; or (d) until the time the accused is sentenced, if applicable"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 517(1): the publication ban. Two functions: the power ("the justice may") and the duty ("and shall on application by the accused"). The ban ends at (a) the discharge at a preliminary inquiry or (b) the end of the trial.
-- src:11535 | Order directing matters not to be published for specified period
-- src:11536 | 517 (1) If the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515, he or she shall so state to the justice and the justice may, and shall on application by the accused, before or at any time during the course of the proceedings under that section, make an order directing that the evidence taken, the information given or the representations made and the reasons, if any, given or to be given by the justice shall not be published in any document, or broadcast or transmitted in any way before such time as
-- src:11537 | (a) if a preliminary inquiry is held, the accused in respect of whom the proceedings are held is discharged; or
-- src:11538 | (b) if the accused in respect of whom the proceedings are held is tried or ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended.
@ref s 517(1) (src:11535-11538)
GIVEN `the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515 and has so stated to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 517(1) the justice may make an order directing that the evidence, information, representations and reasons shall not be published` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515 and has so stated to the justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515, he or she shall so state to the justice and the justice may" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

@ref s 517(1) the duty on the accused's application (src:11536)
GIVEN `the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515 and has so stated to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused applies for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 517(1) the justice must make the order on the application of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor or the accused intends to show cause under section 515 and has so stated to the justice` AND `the accused applies for the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the justice may, and shall on application by the accused"

@ref s 517(1)(a) and (b) (src:11537-11538)
GIVEN `a preliminary inquiry is held and the accused in respect of whom the proceedings are held is discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is tried or ordered to stand trial and the trial is ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 517(1) the order against publication remains in force` MEANS
    IF `a preliminary inquiry is held and the accused in respect of whom the proceedings are held is discharged` OR `the accused is tried or ordered to stand trial and the trial is ended`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be published ... before such time as (a) if a preliminary inquiry is held, the accused in respect of whom the proceedings are held is discharged; or (b) if the accused ... is tried or ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 517(2): "Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with an order made under subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction." The section states no maximum: Part XXVII (outside
-- this range) does, so the Punishment carries "no imprisonment is stated" and "no fine is stated" for this section's own words.
-- src:11539 | Failure to comply
-- src:11540 | (2) Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with an order made under subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 517(2) (src:11539-11540)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 517(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with an order made under subsection (1)` AND NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with an order made under subsection (1) is guilty of an offence"

@ref s 517(2) the class and punishment (src:11540)
`s 517(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 517(2) the class and punishment (src:11540)
`s 517(2) the punishment the section itself states` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:11542 | Inquiries to be made by justice and evidence
-- src:11543 | 518 (1) In any proceedings under section 515,
-- src:11544 | (a) the justice may, subject to paragraph (b), make such inquiries, on oath or otherwise, of and concerning the accused as he considers desirable;
-- src:11545 | (b) the accused shall not be examined by the justice or any other person except counsel for the accused respecting the offence with which the accused is charged, and no inquiry shall be made of the accused respecting that offence by way of cross-examination unless the accused has testified respecting the offence;
-- src:11546 | (c) the prosecutor may, in addition to any other relevant evidence, lead evidence
-- src:11547 | (i) to prove that the accused has previously been convicted of a criminal offence,
-- src:11548 | (ii) to prove that the accused has been charged with and is awaiting trial for another criminal offence,
-- src:11549 | (iii) to prove that the accused has previously committed an offence under section 145, or
-- src:11550 | (iv) to show the circumstances of the alleged offence, particularly as they relate to the probability of conviction of the accused;
-- src:11551 | (d) the justice may take into consideration any relevant matters agreed on by the prosecutor and the accused or his counsel;
-- src:11552 | (d.1) the justice may receive evidence obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI, in writing, orally or in the form of a recording and, for the purposes of this section, subsection 189(5) does not apply to that evidence;
-- src:11553 | (d.2) the justice shall take into consideration any evidence submitted regarding the need to ensure the safety or security of any victim of or witness to an offence; and
-- src:11554 | (e) the justice may receive and base his decision on evidence considered credible or trustworthy by him in the circumstances of each case.
@ref s 518(1) (src:11542-11554)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(a) the justice may make inquiries, on oath or otherwise, of and concerning the accused` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 515`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings under section 515, (a) the justice may ... make such inquiries, on oath or otherwise, of and concerning the accused as he considers desirable" (a "may" outside proceedings under section 515)

@ref s 518(1)(b) (src:11545)
GIVEN `the examination of the accused respects the offence with which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination is by counsel for the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(b) the accused is barred from being examined by the justice or any other person except counsel for the accused` MEANS
    IF `the examination of the accused respects the offence with which the accused is charged` AND NOT `the examination is by counsel for the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the accused shall not be examined by the justice or any other person except counsel for the accused respecting the offence with which the accused is charged"

@ref s 518(1)(b) the cross-examination (src:11545)
GIVEN `the inquiry respects the offence and is by way of cross-examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has testified respecting the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(b) the accused is barred from being cross-examined on the offence` MEANS
    IF `the inquiry respects the offence and is by way of cross-examination` AND NOT `the accused has testified respecting the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no inquiry shall be made of the accused respecting that offence by way of cross-examination unless the accused has testified respecting the offence"

DECLARE `s 518(1)(c) the kind of evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 518(1)(c)(i) evidence to prove that the accused has previously been convicted of a criminal offence`
    `s 518(1)(c)(ii) evidence to prove that the accused has been charged with and is awaiting trial for another criminal offence`
    `s 518(1)(c)(iii) evidence to prove that the accused has previously committed an offence under section 145`
    `s 518(1)(c)(iv) evidence to show the circumstances of the alleged offence, particularly as they relate to the probability of conviction of the accused`
    `s 518(1)(c) other relevant evidence`

@ref s 518(1)(c) (src:11546-11550)
GIVEN evidence IS A `s 518(1)(c) the kind of evidence`
      `the evidence is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(c) the prosecutor may lead the evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER evidence
    WHEN `s 518(1)(c)(i) evidence to prove that the accused has previously been convicted of a criminal offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 518(1)(c)(ii) evidence to prove that the accused has been charged with and is awaiting trial for another criminal offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 518(1)(c)(iii) evidence to prove that the accused has previously committed an offence under section 145` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 518(1)(c)(iv) evidence to show the circumstances of the alleged offence, particularly as they relate to the probability of conviction of the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 518(1)(c) other relevant evidence` THEN
        IF `the evidence is relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the prosecutor may, in addition to any other relevant evidence, lead evidence" says nothing of evidence that is not relevant

@ref s 518(1)(d) (src:11551)
GIVEN `the matters are relevant and agreed on by the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(d) the justice may take the matters into consideration` MEANS
    IF `the matters are relevant and agreed on by the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice may take into consideration any relevant matters agreed on by the prosecutor and the accused or his counsel"

@ref s 518(1)(d.1) (src:11552)
GIVEN `the evidence was obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(d.1) the justice may receive the evidence in writing, orally or as a recording` MEANS
    IF `the evidence was obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice may receive evidence obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI"

@ref s 518(1)(d.1) subsection 189(5) (src:11552)
GIVEN `the evidence was obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(d.1) subsection 189(5) applies to the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence was obtained as a result of an interception of a private communication under and within the meaning of Part VI`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purposes of this section, subsection 189(5) does not apply to that evidence"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (d.1) says only that subsection 189(5) does not apply to that evidence

@ref s 518(1)(d.2) (src:11553)
GIVEN `evidence was submitted regarding the need to ensure the safety or security of any victim of or witness to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(d.2) the justice must take the evidence into consideration` MEANS
    IF `evidence was submitted regarding the need to ensure the safety or security of any victim of or witness to an offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the justice shall take into consideration any evidence submitted regarding the need to ensure the safety or security of any victim of or witness to an offence"

@ref s 518(1)(e) (src:11554)
GIVEN `the justice considers the evidence credible or trustworthy in the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1)(e) the justice may receive the evidence and base the decision on it` MEANS
    IF `the justice considers the evidence credible or trustworthy in the circumstances of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice may receive and base his decision on evidence considered credible or trustworthy by him in the circumstances of each case"

-- src:11555 | Release pending sentence
-- src:11556 | (2) Where, before or at any time during the course of any proceedings under section 515, the accused pleads guilty and that plea is accepted, the justice may make any order provided for in this Part for the release of the accused until the accused is sentenced.
@ref s 518(2) (src:11555-11556)
GIVEN `before or at any time during the course of proceedings under section 515, the accused pleads guilty and that plea is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(2) the justice may make any order provided for in this Part for the release of the accused until sentence` MEANS
    IF `before or at any time during the course of proceedings under section 515, the accused pleads guilty and that plea is accepted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, before or at any time during the course of any proceedings under section 515, the accused pleads guilty and that plea is accepted, the justice may make any order" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

-- src:11557 | Release of accused
-- src:11558 | 519 (1) If a justice makes a release order under section 515,
-- src:11559 | (a) if the accused thereupon complies with the order, the justice shall direct that the accused be released
-- src:11560 | (i) forthwith, if the accused is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter, or
-- src:11561 | (ii) as soon thereafter as the accused is no longer required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter;
-- src:11562 | (b) if the accused does not thereupon comply with the order, the justice who made the order or another justice having jurisdiction shall issue a warrant for the committal of the accused and may endorse thereon an authorization to the person having the custody of the accused to release the accused when the accused complies with the order
-- src:11563 | (i) forthwith after the compliance, if the accused is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter, or
-- src:11564 | (ii) as soon thereafter as the accused is no longer required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter
-- src:11565 | and if the justice so endorses the warrant, he shall attach to it a copy of the order; and
-- src:11566 | (c) any condition in the order that an accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions, is effective from the moment it is made, whether or not the accused has been released from custody.
-- src:11567 | Discharge from custody
-- src:11568 | (2) Where the accused complies with an order referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter, the justice who made the order or another justice having jurisdiction shall, unless the accused has been or will be released pursuant to an authorization referred to in that paragraph, issue an order for discharge in Form 39.
@ref s 519(1) and (2) (src:11557-11568)
GIVEN `the justice makes a release order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused thereupon complies with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1)(a) the justice must direct that the accused be released forthwith` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes a release order under section 515` AND `the accused thereupon complies with the order` AND NOT `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)(i)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the accused thereupon complies with the order, the justice shall direct that the accused be released (i) forthwith, if the accused is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter"

@ref s 519(1)(a)(ii) (src:11561)
GIVEN `the justice makes a release order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused thereupon complies with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1)(a) the justice must direct that the accused be released as soon as the accused is no longer required to be detained in respect of another matter` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes a release order under section 515` AND `the accused thereupon complies with the order` AND `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)(ii)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) as soon thereafter as the accused is no longer required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter"

@ref s 519(1)(b) (src:11562-11565)
GIVEN `the justice makes a release order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused does not thereupon comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1)(b) the justice who made the order or another justice having jurisdiction must issue a warrant for the committal of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes a release order under section 515` AND `the accused does not thereupon comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the accused does not thereupon comply with the order, the justice who made the order or another justice having jurisdiction shall issue a warrant for the committal of the accused"

@ref s 519(1)(b) the copy (src:11565)
GIVEN `the justice endorses the warrant with an authorization to release the accused when the accused complies with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1)(b) the justice must attach a copy of the order to the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the justice endorses the warrant with an authorization to release the accused when the accused complies with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if the justice so endorses the warrant, he shall attach to it a copy of the order"

@ref s 519(1)(c) (src:11566)
GIVEN `the order contains a condition that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1)(c) the no-communication condition is effective from the moment it is made, whether or not the accused has been released from custody` MEANS
    IF `the order contains a condition that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) says when a no-communication condition takes effect and says nothing of any other condition

@ref s 519(2) (src:11567-11568)
GIVEN `the accused complies with an order referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been or will be released pursuant to an authorization referred to in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(2) the justice must issue an order for discharge in Form 39` MEANS
    IF `the accused complies with an order referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` AND `the accused is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` AND NOT `the accused has been or will be released pursuant to an authorization referred to in that paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the accused complies with an order referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter, the justice ... shall, unless the accused has been or will be released pursuant to an authorization referred to in that paragraph, issue an order for discharge in Form 39"

-- src:11569 | Warrant for committal
-- src:11570 | (3) Where the justice makes an order under subsection 515(5) or (6) for the detention of the accused, he shall issue a warrant for the committal of the accused.
@ref s 519(3) (src:11569-11570)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order under subsection 515(5) or (6) for the detention of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(3) the justice must issue a warrant for the committal of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order under subsection 515(5) or (6) for the detention of the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the justice makes an order under subsection 515(5) or (6) for the detention of the accused, he shall issue a warrant for the committal of the accused"

-- src:11571 | Variation of release order with consent
-- src:11572 | 519.1 A release order under which an accused has been released under section 515 may be varied with the written consent of the accused, prosecutor and any sureties. The order so varied is considered to be a release order under section 515.
@ref s 519.1 (src:11571-11572)
GIVEN `the accused has been released under a release order under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every surety consents in writing (true where there is no surety)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519.1 the release order may be varied` MEANS
    IF `the accused has been released under a release order under section 515` AND `the accused consents in writing` AND `the prosecutor consents in writing` AND `every surety consents in writing (true where there is no surety)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A release order ... may be varied with the written consent of the accused, prosecutor and any sureties" (a "may" whose gate fails)

@ref s 519.1 the second sentence (src:11572)
GIVEN `the release order was varied under section 519.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519.1 the varied order is considered to be a release order under section 515` MEANS
    IF `the release order was varied under section 519.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The order so varied is considered to be a release order under section 515" says nothing of an order not so varied
